{:edb/db-before-t 1281 :edb/db-after-t 1282 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534594 50 #inst "2026-10-08T01:55:17.265Z" 13194139534594 true] [17592186064174 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297708 13194139534594 true] [17592186064174 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297729 13194139534594 true] [17592186064175 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297715 13194139534594 true] [17592186064175 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297722 13194139534594 true] [17592186064860 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534594 true] [17592186064860 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nA particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t) = 9$, where $t$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x = 0$ when $t = 1$, calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t > 0$." 13194139534594 false] [17592186064860 1100 "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)=9,$ where $t$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=0$ when $t=1,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t>0.$" 13194139534594 true] [17592186064860 1145 "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 9\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =9t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $x(1)=0.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =9(1)+C \\\\ C & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=9t-9.\n$$" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297708 1017 #edb/ref 17592186297709 13194139534594 true] [17592186297708 1089 "q-102782" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297708 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534594 true] [17592186297708 1100 "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t),$ where $t$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=3$ when $t=0,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t>0.$" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297708 1113 #uuid "082878d7-c949-5c37-b9d7-9ff7084bdec8" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297708 1145 "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $x(0)=3.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(0))+C \\\\ 3 & =0+C \\\\ C & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nx(t)=3+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t).\n$$" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297710 13194139534594 true] [17592186297709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297711 13194139534594 true] [17592186297709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297712 13194139534594 true] [17592186297709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297713 13194139534594 true] [17592186297709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297714 13194139534594 true] [17592186297709 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534594 true] [17592186297709 1041 "selection" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297709 1104 #edb/ref 17592186297713 13194139534594 true] [17592186297709 1110 #uuid "d660a1eb-0875-5b4e-9e0f-6c115720c422" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297710 1034 "x(t)=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t+3)" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297710 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534594 true] [17592186297710 1111 #uuid "01818edb-894c-5485-b72f-2e8d3dcef054" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297711 1034 "x(t)=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297711 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534594 true] [17592186297711 1111 #uuid "9aa4d5c6-46be-5b73-9645-fc2a754ea4b6" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297712 1034 "x(t)=3-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297712 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534594 true] [17592186297712 1111 #uuid "f5993b90-47b7-5904-b623-ee0dabe128b3" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297713 1034 "x(t)=3+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297713 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534594 true] [17592186297713 1111 #uuid "b7e49faf-6828-5752-b7ea-5e9c5dd3527a" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297714 1034 "x(t)=3+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297714 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534594 true] [17592186297714 1111 #uuid "2e3bd353-87d7-56ef-ba7f-3bcb6e3ca373" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297715 1017 #edb/ref 17592186297716 13194139534594 true] [17592186297715 1089 "q-102993" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297715 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534594 true] [17592186297715 1100 "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration $a(t)=\\frac{4}{(t+1)^{3}}$, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time. If the particle has position $x=1$ and velocity $v=-\\frac{1}{2}$ when $t=1$, calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t>0.$" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297715 1113 #uuid "086db544-da02-585a-9178-5af9c52946c7" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297715 1145 "We start by integrating the acceleration to get the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{4}{(t+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{(t+1)^{2}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(1)=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & =-\\frac{2}{(1+1)^{2}}+C \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & =-\\frac{1}{2}+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the velocity is given by $v(t)=-\\frac{2}{(t+1)^{2}}.$ \n\nNow, we integrate the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (-\\frac{2}{(t+1)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{t+1}+K\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $K$, we use the fact that $x(1)=1.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\frac{2}{1+1}+K \\\\ 1 & =1+K \\\\ K & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{2}{t+1}.\n$$" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297716 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297717 13194139534594 true] [17592186297716 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297718 13194139534594 true] [17592186297716 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297719 13194139534594 true] [17592186297716 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297720 13194139534594 true] [17592186297716 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297721 13194139534594 true] [17592186297716 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534594 true] [17592186297716 1041 "selection" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297716 1104 #edb/ref 17592186297721 13194139534594 true] [17592186297716 1110 #uuid "34c88a64-9e02-5f60-9497-308b7b4648cb" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297717 1034 "x(t)=\\frac{1}{t+1}+\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297717 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534594 true] [17592186297717 1111 #uuid "f995afe7-724e-5ef1-a928-f1407e6a5677" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297718 1034 "x(t)=\\frac{2}{t+1}-1" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297718 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534594 true] [17592186297718 1111 #uuid "f531d080-f85f-5752-b424-8850ab35296f" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297719 1034 "x(t)=\\frac{4}{(t+1)^{2}}" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297719 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534594 true] [17592186297719 1111 #uuid "7fd90584-fc8d-50bb-96eb-f78fedd8cea8" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297720 1034 "x(t)=\\frac{2}{(t+1)^{2}}" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297720 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534594 true] [17592186297720 1111 #uuid "4d0e0a0c-dbfc-58b6-8260-1eb622b6709f" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297721 1034 "x(t)=\\frac{2}{t+1}" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297721 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534594 true] [17592186297721 1111 #uuid "61b0fb92-917f-5071-9363-078fd0810643" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297722 1017 #edb/ref 17592186297723 13194139534594 true] [17592186297722 1089 "q-102994" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297722 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534594 true] [17592186297722 1100 "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration $a(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)$, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time. If the particle has position $x=\\frac{1}{16}$ and velocity $v=\\frac{1}{4}$ when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$, calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t>0.$" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297722 1113 #uuid "8985ff83-3d60-5f09-b241-0ff8efcd199d" 13194139534594 true] [17592186297722 1145 "We start by integrating the acceleration to get the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=\\frac{1}{4}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{1}{4}+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the velocity is given by $v(t)=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t).$ \n\nNow, we integrate the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+K\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $K,$ we use the fact that $x(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=\\frac{1}{16}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{16} & =-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{16} & =-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{16} & =0+C \\\\ K & =\\frac{1}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\frac{1}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t))\\end{aligned}\n$$" 1319413953459